<section class="about-ribbon" aria-label="StudyHub principles"><div><strong>01</strong><span>Make room for the work</span></div><div><strong>02</strong><span>Keep the room human</span></div><div><strong>03</strong><span>Leave the data alone</span></div></section>
<section class="about-manifesto" aria-label="StudyHub mission"><div class="manifesto-mark"><i data-lucide="asterisk"></i><span>THE POINT</span></div><h2>School is hard enough.<br><em>The tools should be kind.</em></h2><div class="manifesto-rule"></div><p>Less performance. More progress. Less noise. More room to think.</p></section>
<section class="public-section split-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHY WE EXIST</p><h2>Schoolwork is shared work.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>StudyHub exists to make the everyday coordination around school less noisy: a deadline, a question, a shared resource, or a small project group should not require five scattered tools.</p><p>We are building this as a not-for-profit project. That means the product is organized around usefulness and access rather than advertising revenue or maximizing time spent.</p></div></section>
<section class="public-section"><p class="eyebrow">OUR COMMITMENTS</p><div class="icon-grid"><article><i data-lucide="shield-check"></i><h3>Strict moderation</h3><p>Titles, tasks, comments, resources, and shared links are screened. Members can report content, and moderators can remove content, warn, suspend, or ban accounts.</p></article><article><i data-lucide="school"></i><h3>Student-centered</h3><p>We keep the interface focused on classes, deadlines, groups, and useful peer context instead of feeds designed to keep you scrolling.</p></article><article><i data-lucide="lock-keyhole"></i><h3>Respect for privacy</h3><p>We collect the information needed to run the workspace. Accounts use usernames rather than email addresses today, and personal todos are encrypted at rest.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="public-section goals-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHERE WE ARE GOING</p><h2>Useful, humane, and accountable.</h2></div><ul class="check-list"><li><i data-lucide="check"></i> Make group study easier without making students perform online.</li><li><i data-lucide="check"></i> Keep moderation understandable, consistent, and reviewable.</li><li><i data-lucide="check"></i> Add carefully chosen features without turning student work into a product.</li></ul></section>